# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. STAGING, material not yet scrubbed. Present on disk, never committed.
#    A .gitignore protects git, not `cp -r`. Extraction copies, so verify by size:
#    a tree far larger than its file listing means something came along.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/staging/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. The real-value denylist must live OUTSIDE any repo. Belt and braces:
#    the gate refuses to run if MW_DENYLIST points inside the tree.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
denylist.txt
*denylist*.txt
!DENYLIST.example.txt

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. Anything a person's own matter might arrive as. Nothing in this repository
#    ever needs one of these, so an accidental copy is always a mistake.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.pdf
*.epub
*.eml
*.mbox
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4. Machine and editor state. A real username survives in these constantly,
#    and a path with a real username in it is an attribution leak.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
._*
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.log
.env
.env.*

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 5. Node is a BUILD tool only (ADR 0007 decision 10). Nothing here ships a
#    dependency; the build-time YAML parser is a devDependency and its install
#    tree is never committed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 6. 🔴 CLAUDE.md AND .claude/ ARE TRACKED IN THIS REPOSITORY, deliberately, and
#    this is a reversal of the rule the previous repository shape used.
#
#    There, both were workspace-local agent state and ignoring them was correct.
#    Here, ADR 0007 makes them authored and generated PRODUCT:
#      · CLAUDE.md is the instruction file an agent working ON this repo reads.
#      · .claude/ and .codex/ are GENERATED provider trees. The freshness check
#        rebuilds them and diffs against what is committed, so ignoring them
#        would make that check compare a build against nothing, green on zero
#        scanned bytes, which is this project's headline failure mode.
#    ⚠️ .claude/ is generated. Hand-editing it fails the freshness check; edit
#       skill/ and rebuild.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 7. ⚖️ The per-install jurisdiction note. WRITTEN BY THE ASSISTANT after `init`,
#    never by the engine, and never committed. ADR 0008 decision 5, AGENTS.md §8.
#
#    It exists so a later session does not ask a frightened person to remember a
#    two-letter code they were shown once. It is per-install by definition, so
#    committing it would ship one person's answer to everybody who cloned this.
#
#    ⚠️ A .gitignore IS NOT A SECURITY BOUNDARY, and this one least of all. It
#    does not stop a forced add, a parent repository, a backup tool, or a search
#    index. That is exactly why the case folder's PATH is not allowed in this
#    file: the opt-in pointer screen makes writing a path down a deliberate,
#    off-by-default choice, and a note that recorded it anyway would defeat that
#    screen quietly, which is worse than not having the note at all.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.mw/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 8. 🔴 RUNTIME ARTIFACTS THAT LAND IN THE CURRENT DIRECTORY, and the reason they
#    are listed here is a MISDIAGNOSIS rather than tidiness.
#
#    `.mw/` above is a DIRECTORY pattern and does not match a FILE. The engine
#    writes `.mw-state.json` into the working directory before a workspace has
#    been confirmed, so one run anywhere in this tree leaves it behind.
#
#    CI's generated-tree-fresh check requires `git status --porcelain` to be
#    EMPTY. So a single stray engine run turns CI red while NAMING THE GENERATED
#    TREE AS STALE, which is a true symptom pointing at a false cause. Anyone
#    reading that would go and "fix" scripts/build.mjs, which is not broken, and
#    the trap arrives precisely when someone is already editing it.
#
#    Same shape for the two evaluation artifacts: a skill-evaluation arc writes
#    `evals/` inside the skill directory and a sibling `<name>-workspace/`, and
#    evaluating this skill RUNS it, which writes the state file again.
#
#    ⚠️ As with section 7: not a security boundary. It stops an accident, not a
#    forced add, and `.mw-state.json` is per-person state that must never ship.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.mw-state.json
evals/
*-workspace/
